{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360235-mage-armour-and-surprise-attack-2e","id":1360235,"title":"Mage Armour and Surprise Attack [2e]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-10T17:32:07-08:00","id":1360235,"title":"Mage Armour and Surprise Attack [2e]","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The rulebook says: Mage Armors that increase Defense work against surprise attacks.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Does this apply the whole defence or just the defence added by the armour?</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8037-leyoz","name":"Leyoz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-10T17:36:45-08:00","id":1360237,"title":"","content":"The latter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> only the bonus points granted by the Magic Armor. (Save some powerfull spell or merit say otherwise)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T11:26:50-08:00","id":1360562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360235-mage-armour-and-surprise-attack-2e?p=1360237#post1360237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The latter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> only the bonus points granted by the Magic Armor. (Save some powerfull spell or merit say otherwise)</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. You still have a defence rating when surprised you just cant use it. Your defence does not drop to 0 when surprised. Mage armour increases your defence AND lets you use that new full rating vs surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T12:06:34-08:00","id":1360564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360235-mage-armour-and-surprise-attack-2e?p=1360562#post1360562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong. You still have a defence rating when surprised you just cant use it. Your defence does not drop to 0 when surprised. Mage armour increases your defence AND lets you use that new full rating vs surprise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you point the page on the book, please?<br /> <br /> On the Core i read this, 193<br /> &quot; A mage can only benefit from one form of<br /> Mage Armor at a time, but can spend Mana to change between<br /> Arcana as a reflexive action. Mage Armors that increase Defense<br /> work against surprise attacks&quot; pp 193<br /> <br /> And<br /> &quot; Surprise<br /> Characters who don\u2019t realize that they\u2019re about to be on the<br /> receiving end of bloody violence have a chance to notice the<br /> ambush by rolling Wits + Composure, contested by the attacker\u2019s<br /> Dexterity + Stealth. Any character who fails the roll cannot take<br /> an action in the first turn of combat, and can\u2019t apply Defense<br /> for that turn. Determine Initiative in the second turn as normal.&quot; pp 217","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T14:30:16-08:00","id":1360593,"title":"","content":"Failing the roll and being surprised means you cannot apply defense, it does not say that defense drops to zero. Therefore mage armour both increases your normal and <u><i>only</i></u> defense and that then works against surprise attacks.<br /> <br /> I can't show you where it says it drops your defense to zero which is what would happen if you only got to apply mage armour as there is no such text.<br /> <br /> You only have one defense rating which mage armor increases and then works against surprise attacks, you dont have 2 defense rating, one not able to apply to surprise and one that does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-12-2020, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T04:08:20-08:00","id":1360669,"title":"","content":"I never said &quot;there is two defence rating&quot;. Only that some mage armor give a bonus to Defence <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If surprised, you have only the bonus from Mage Armor. I dont found written: &quot;Mage Armor grant your Defence also on surprise.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 01-13-2020, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T06:08:04-08:00","id":1360683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360235-mage-armour-and-surprise-attack-2e?p=1360669#post1360669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said &quot;there is two defence rating&quot;. Only that some mage armor give a bonus to Defence <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> If surprised, you have only the bonus from Mage Armor. I dont found written: &quot;Mage Armor grant your Defence also on surprise.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>When surprised you normally do not get to apply your defense rating. Mage armors that increase defense (which include: Fate, Mind, Life, Space and Time) work vs surprise.<br /> So what happens when you activate one of these 5 mage armors? Well you add some bonus X to your defense. There is no separate stat called &quot;mage armor X&quot; that you could apply separately vs a surprise attack the only thing you can apply is just the defense rating which is not modified by the mage armor.<br /> Therefore if you are surprised while having of these mage armors on you get to apply your defense rating to the persons attack as normal. Your defense rating while under one of these armors is<br /> usually &quot;lowest of wits/dex + athletics&quot; + &quot;arcana rating&quot;. You cant separate the bonus given to defense and use that vs a surprise attack.<br /> <br /> If you have 7 defense and gain 3 from mage armor then you have defense 10. There no 3 to use vs a surprise attack because like i've said you cant split the defense up like that. You have defense 10 and are using one<br /> of the mage armors that work vs surprise and that mage armor modified your defense which is what is used vs an attack.<br /> <br /> Had the text been &quot;the bonus gained from mage armours that add to defense works against surprise attacks&quot; then you would be correct but it only identifies what armors work vs surprise and it isnt a condition that the mage armors bonus only works vs surprise.<br /> <br /> The &quot;works vs&quot; text could be clearer tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-13-2020, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T06:55:31-08:00","id":1360686,"title":"","content":"Perhaps <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> can give his words for sake of clarity? This is the first time that i see this interpretation, but, this is no proof that you are wrong neither.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T09:58:49-08:00","id":1360703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Throne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360235-mage-armour-and-surprise-attack-2e?p=1360686#post1360686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a> can give his words for sake of clarity? This is the first time that i see this interpretation, but, this is no proof that you are wrong neither.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not going to happen. Dave almost never responds to pings about stuff like this. Think about, if he did respond to it he would get bugged for rulings about this kind of thing -all- the time. He\u2019s also not the line dev anymore, so I imagine he\u2019ll want to spare himself the headache of getting involved.<br /> <br /> Just make a ruling that makes sense to you and move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T10:19:13-08:00","id":1360705,"title":"","content":"Sometime he answer , sometime not. I tried this only one time , dont ask for anything <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I am cool as i saied. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T15:57:50-08:00","id":1360778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360235-mage-armour-and-surprise-attack-2e?p=1360683#post1360683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is no separate stat called &quot;mage armor X&quot; that you could apply separately vs a surprise attack the only thing you can apply is just the defense rating which is not modified by the mage armor.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, however, implicit precedent in the system for calculating Defense differently in varying situations, such as Defense vs Firearms - people often think of this as a binary state where you either have Defense vs Firearms or don't, but in reality I can think of at least two systems off the top of my head that give you some measure of Defense vs Firearms without allowing you to include your full Defense rating (or leaning on it at all).<br /> <br /> It is not entirely unreasonable to lean on that precedent to calculate Defense vs surprise attacks, but I'd agree that the raw text doesn't particularly strongly support that interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T20:33:10-08:00","id":1360807,"title":"","content":"You still have a defense rating when dealing with firearms, you just cant normally apply it. <br /> <br /> Calculating it differently would then be explicitly mentioned (which systems are there). <br /> <br /> The issue is just then interpretation of what &quot;works Vs surprise&quot; means.<br /> <br /> General armor works Vs surprise attacks s you go look at your armor rating and say ok I have general armor of X. Applying that for defense MAs you would say I have defense 10 instead of 7 with it on. I just think if defense for surprise with MA on changed how you calculated defense it would/should say so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-13-2020, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T09:28:51-08:00","id":1360897,"title":"","content":"I'd say that only the bonus defence from the armour is applied to the surprise attack, not the entirety of your defence. After all, it is pretty explicitly talking about the Mage Armour when it says &quot;Mage Armors that increase Defense work against surprise attacks&quot;. And if you think about it, it makes sense. You're not actually dodging the blow if you're using Space mage armour, space is just distorted and causes the blow to miss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12968-necrosx","name":"Necrosx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12968_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T15:02:42-08:00","id":1360962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360235-mage-armour-and-surprise-attack-2e?p=1360807#post1360807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think if defense for surprise with MA on changed how you calculated defense it <b>should</b> say so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360235-mage-armour-and-surprise-attack-2e?p=1360807#post1360807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just think if defense for surprise with MA on changed how you calculated defense it <b>w</b><b>ould</b> say so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T22:26:37-08:00","id":1361012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necrosx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360235-mage-armour-and-surprise-attack-2e?p=1360897#post1360897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that only the bonus defence from the armour is applied to the surprise attack, not the entirety of your defence. After all, it is pretty explicitly talking about the Mage Armour when it says &quot;Mage Armors that increase Defense work against surprise attacks&quot;. And if you think about it, it makes sense. You're not actually dodging the blow if you're using Space mage armour, space is just distorted and causes the blow to miss.</div> </div> </div> </div>MA's that add to defense are not separate things though. If we ignore the reference to surprise attacks then they &quot;work&quot; by applying a bonus to defense and become part of that defense value. Extending how they &quot;work&quot; Vs surprise then implies full defense value.<br /> <br /> One also wonders that when surprised you can't take any actions, does this include the reflexive for MA meaning you need it up beforehand, or does the &quot;work Vs surprise&quot; statement also cover being able to turn it on while surprised. Which I assume it does otherwise you'd need to have MA up before being surprised for it to matter.<br /> <br /> So the &quot;works Vs surprise&quot; statement seems to mean, you can take an action you normally can't and apply your defense when you normally can't.<br /> <br /> But play it how you like, I think I've written enough text about it for a lifetime. I'm still amazed that years after its been finished multiple interpretations from what my friends who hate on nwod call &quot;bad or sloppy&quot; writing still crop up.<br /> <br /> But then my response is at least it doesn't read like the hero rulebook which reads like a technical manual..<br /> <br /> A similar problem occurs when using firearms in close combat. Its says defense is <i>increased</i> by guns size+1 (not becomes gun size +1) yet normally you dont apply defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-15-2020, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-16T16:41:13-08:00","id":1368430,"title":"","content":"So I have found somebody else asking this question years ago on rpg.net where the answer from dave was that when surprised people only get the mage armor part. So it seems that is the correct interpretation of it, however, badly conveyed it is. &quot;Characters with mage armor that increases defense can use the bonus even while surprised.&quot; would have been clearer? Though &quot;works vs surprise&quot; must also let you use a reflexive action to turn mage armor on, otherwise you'd need it up before being surprised, which might be intentional, I'm unsure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T10:44:49-08:00","id":1368571,"title":"","content":"Personally I find it pretty straightforward that's the way it works. Reading it differently seems like mental gimnastics.<br /> <br /> If it allowed you to apply defense where you couldn't it would most likely specifically say so (like Acceleration does) instead of using the phrasing it currently uses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","user":"Menace","date":". 02-17-2020, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-17T17:32:50-08:00","id":1368648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360235-mage-armour-and-surprise-attack-2e?p=1368571#post1368571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I find it pretty straightforward that's the way it works. Reading it differently seems like mental gimnastics.<br /> <br /> If it allowed you to apply defense where you couldn't it would most likely specifically say so (like Acceleration does) instead of using the phrasing it currently uses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrongly i always assumed mages could reflexively activate mage armor on the turn they get surprised.(reading too many &quot;haha i can snipe a mage vs no you cant cos mage armor&quot; arguments no doubt.) The &quot;works vs surprise&quot; text is just allowing you to use already active mage armors that increase defense to be useful while surprised. Active matter armor giving 3 armor when surprised vs active fate armor without the text saying it works vs surprise would do nothing since it would be increasing something you couldn't then use when surprised. Makes sense now.<br /> <br /> It does give the &quot;surprise snipe&quot; argument more weight though and also meaning you need to have mage armor active in more situations (read even slightly risky situations) than i thought before (since you didnt need to activate it until you got surprised) means that while pretty easy to replenish mages probably spend more mana than i assumed. It also means you'd put mage armor on if even there was a hint of a trap or any surprise whereas before i thought being able to reflexively activate it before a trap explodes you may not bother until it did happen..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-23T04:59:40-08:00","id":1369813,"title":"","content":"It used to be in 1st edition that you could just always have Mage Armor (and sight) on all the time, that's propably where the comments came from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}